From b4c9ee0ebe977722a45d58649747e28077ac0429 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenAI <openai@example.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 22:55:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: match GPON NBOQ to T-CONT channel

The EN7523 vendor GPON transmit path programs both the QDMA channel
and the NBOQ sideband field from the GEM port T-CONT channel. The
current driver only programs the channel in msg0 while leaving NBOQ
tied to the static GDM netdev value, which is zero for the xPON GDM2
netdev. This produces mismatched channel metadata for service T-CONTs.

Use the classified T-CONT channel for NBOQ on xPON packets. OMCI
traffic remains on channel zero, while non-xPON users retain the
existing netdev NBOQ selection.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI <openai@example.com>
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
index c8b1a67c2..487233bb1 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -3758,7 +3758,8 @@ static netdev_tx_t __airoha_dev_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb,
 	}
 
 	fport = airoha_get_fe_port(dev);
-	msg1 = FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_NBOQ_MASK, dev->nbq) |
+	msg1 = FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_NBOQ_MASK,
+			  xpon ? xpon->tcont : dev->nbq) |
 	       FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_FPORT_MASK, fport) |
 	       FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_METER_MASK, 0x7f);
 	if (xpon_oam)
